/target
*.proptest-regressions

# crates/firmware is its own workspace (excluded from the root one, see the
# root Cargo.toml), so its build output lands in a separate target/ dir that
# the root-only /target rule above does not reach.
/crates/firmware/target

# Real device backups carry radio addresses + rolling codes — never commit them.
# The fixtures README stays tracked; the exported capture does not.
crates/somfy-migrate/tests/fixtures/*.backup

# Agent worktrees created by EnterWorktree/isolation, never part of the project.
.claude/

# Web UI (Plan 7). The lockfile IS tracked; installed packages and build output
# are not. `dist/` is produced by `bun run build` and consumed by the xtask that
# embeds it in the firmware image, so it is a build artefact like /target.
/ui/node_modules
/ui/dist
